## 4. Negative-control proof

The launcher runs the real reported screenshot OCR sequence with test-only expected `damage=87313`; the expected ground truth is `87373`. OCR itself completed and returned the real damage value, the comparison failed, and the sequence exited with code `1`. The acceptance launcher counted this negative test as a pass only after verifying the JSON report had `comparison.damage.pass === false` and `allExpectedFieldsPass === false`. This confirms a deliberate expected-value mismatch fails closed in the actual sequence path, not merely in a unit-level comparator.

